# Search-tool overrides. This file is NOT a git mechanism — git never reads it.
# It is read by ripgrep and the tools built on it, where it outranks .gitignore.
#
# spec/ is git-ignored (see .gitignore) but must stay searchable, so coding
# agents can index it and @-mention its files. Only negating the directory
# itself works: nothing beneath an excluded directory can be re-included, so
# `!spec/**` and `!spec/*.md` both silently fail where `!spec/` succeeds.
!spec/
